type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.\n", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Mercury Retrograde", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "That's Just Silly Talk!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 17, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Exchange information about hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">That</span>-Clauses: With or Without Personal Objects", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " After some verbs, you can use a <span class=\"italic\">that</span>-clause with or without a personal object before that. If you do include an object, you need to add a preposition before it.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">admitted (to me) that</span> she stole the bag.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">pointed out (to the tour guide) that </span>we missed the turn.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use these verbs in the same way: <span class=\"italic\">announce, complain, confess, explain, indicate, mention, propose, recommend, report, say, suggest.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "After some verbs, you use <span class=\"italic\">with</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">agreed (with James) that</span> the information should be kept secret.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use these verbs in the same way: <span class=\"italic\">argue, check, disagree, joke</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You mentioned that it affects personal communication.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She claimed that she had lots of experience but I'm beginning to doubt her. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I explained that she would have to work weekends but now she's saying that she can't.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You recommended that I not make any changes during the retrograde but I didn't heed your warning.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Speculating About the Past with Different Degrees of Certainty", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You make decisions and conclusions using the information that is available to you. You may be more or less certain of your conclusion depending on this information.  You can use different modals to indicate how certain your conclusion is.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If you have strong evidence, and are fairly certain about actions that occurred in the past, you use <span class=\"strong\">must have</span> and <span class=\"strong\">couldn't have</span> plus the past participle of the verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you speculate that something <span class=\"underline\">did</span> happen, you use <span class=\"italic\">must have + past participle</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Nancy has a tan - she <span class=\"strong\">must have traveled</span> to a warm and sunny place.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you speculate that something <span class=\"underline\">did not</span> happen, you use <span class=\"italic\">must not have + past participle</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">must not have cleaned</span> his room because there is still laundry everywhere!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you speculate that something was possible but you are less certain, you use <span class=\"italic\">could have + past participle</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you speculate that something <span class=\"underline\">was impossible</span>, you use <span class=\"italic\">can't have + past participle </span>or <span class=\"italic\">could not have + past participle</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Jessica <span class=\"strong\">couldn't have taken</span> your bag - she wasn't even here today!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I think the retrograde could have affected me after all.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That can't all have been a coincidence.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It must have been caused by the Mercury retrograde. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That could have been a bad idea. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If we weren't in Mercury retrograde, all of that wouldn't have happened at the same time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When you want to talk about something that didn't happen, but you want to imagine that it did, you can use <span class=\"italic\">would (not) have + past participle</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">It's likely that if we weren't in Mercury retrograde, all of that wouldn't have happened at the same time.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to embark", "type": "name"}, {"content": "begin", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You don't want to embark on anything new if Mercury is in retrograde.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about coincidences.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "out of character", "type": "name"}, {"content": "inconsistent with usual patterns of behaviour", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  If people do and say things that are out of character during this time, you have to take them with a grain of salt. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to doubt", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to feel uncertain", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She claimed that she had lots of experience but I'm beginning to doubt her.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "magnetic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "attracting by the properties of a magnet", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You talked about the magnetic effect on electronic equipment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to recall", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bbring the \u200bmemory of a past \u200bevent into \u200byour \u200bmind", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I recalled that my internet got really slow and my laptop was doing strange things. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to go kaput", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to no longer work or be effective", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My microwave oven went kaput.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to heed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to pay attention to advice or warnings", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You recommended that I not make any changes during the retrograde but I didn't heed your warning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pay the price", "type": "name"}, {"content": "suffering the consequences of one's actions", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Now I think I'm paying the price.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le17ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think about a time that you had to eat your words (admit that what you said was wrong).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a story about the situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you can't think of a true story you can make one up.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your story aloud to your class or group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Decide together who had the funniest, most embarrassing or craziest story.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a story about when I was wrong.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my story to a group.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I listen to other students' stories.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I decide on the funniest, most embarrassing or craziest story with my group.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena"}